            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0851" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg771"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/194: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sydney</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sydney</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-27T11:00:00+10:00">October 27,
                            1936—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 28—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Government’s trade diversion is to be debated in Parliament November 4th and 5th.
                    Every indication points to approval by substantial majority.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moffat</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
